All of CARR's fixed settings are given with concrete values, enough to reproduce the protocol. These include:
- nugget 1e-8; log a bounds [-7,7]; tolerance 1e-5;
- refresh at n=10 and every 10 observations; three arrival-mod-3 folds;
- the six experts with their settings (64 neighbours, smoothing 1e-8, 32 trees with leaf size 1, knot formula, ridge 1e-5/1e-4, leaf-size rule, asinh s0 rule with [-30,30] clip);
- SLSQP tolerance 1e-10 and 200 iterations; penalty 1e-6;
- k∈{3,8,16,32}, η∈{0,…,1}, clip ranges and floors;
- M=512 integration points; candidate pool 256 Sobol + 16 per face + corners + ≤64 midpoints.
The fitted quantities (weights, λ, η) are reported per function in Table 7.
